"""Leading with AI (Leadership Edition), Session 11: Redesigning work: workflows, value and the business case (practical).  Written 12 November 2026.

Based on Executive Session 12 (workflow mapping), stripped of maths: the business case is worked in words, tables and shillings.  Pattern of a practical:
recall and a hook; the idea (workflow, map, four kinds of help, three kinds of value) with the industry tour and three cases; a worked example
(the recorded rule against AI comparison, then the Nile Valley Foods business case in shillings and the portfolio scoring); 60 minutes of the
leader's own work; people and the decision; the take-away.

Cases (research/*.md): ADO-02 MIT NANDA, ADO-08 PwC Africa, ADO-03 Gartner 30% (hook); EDU-05 Georgia State, MFG-07 Unilever, ENR-03 Shell and
AGR-07 One Acre Fund (three kinds of value; AGR-07 added because the plan has no case of time saved by redesigning a check); BNK-07 Capitec,
TEL-03 Safaricom, AGR-07, MFG-07, HLT-02 Jacaranda Health, PUB-01 URA (tour); MFG-03 Coca-Cola, MFG-07 Unilever, PUB-01 URA (case stories).
Demonstration (reused, not rerun): demo_runs/s12_rule_vs_ai.md, from the Executive Edition's Twelve-Message AI Demonstration Results (4 Nov 2026):
AI Claude, three fresh sessions, 4 November 2026, 9 of 12 exact, 11 of 12 acceptable; keyword rule 7 of 12 (computed).
Business case: the grey NVF example of Templates/Business Case Workbook.xlsx, recomputed by demo_runs/s12/business_case_check.py and
teaching_numbers_check.py (plan figures, invented inputs).  The portfolio scores on the grid slide are illustrative.
"""

